WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.410
{Chapter 01}

00:14.740 --> 00:17.749
That reminds me, Sawaguchi
was complaining before.

00:17.750 --> 00:22.500
He doesn't want to be a senior
or have to retire from the team.

00:22.920 --> 00:23.960
What about you?

00:24.750 --> 00:26.510
You think about stuff like that?

00:27.880 --> 00:31.259
There's no point in
thinking about the future.

00:31.260 --> 00:32.969
I see.

00:32.970 --> 00:35.139
It's pretty normal to think about.

00:35.140 --> 00:39.140
Didn't you say you wanted to go to Koshien?

00:41.310 --> 00:42.810
A year ago, I did.

00:43.860 --> 00:46.440
But I can't even think about that now.

00:47.280 --> 00:48.530
I'm too tired.

00:49.700 --> 00:54.910
Just thinking about being stuck with
you in high school is all I can handle.

00:56.370 --> 00:57.410
Gou.

00:57.700 --> 00:58.960
Why did you come back?

01:02.040 --> 01:05.670
Why did you want to be my catcher again?

01:09.170 --> 01:12.180
Do you want to be friends
with me or something?

01:15.430 --> 01:18.430
What's the reason you put that mitt on?

01:21.890 --> 01:22.890
Takumi.

01:24.360 --> 01:26.480
The pitch you threw to Kaionji...

01:27.860 --> 01:28.860
was that?

01:52.090 --> 01:57.640
I've heard it said so many times

01:58.390 --> 02:04.560
How it's not going to work out

02:05.520 --> 02:11.070
That nothing will change

02:11.360 --> 02:17.530
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:17.990 --> 02:21.369
I knew it all

02:21.370 --> 02:24.539
I learned this from you

02:24.540 --> 02:32.540
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:33.930 --> 02:40.519
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:40.520 --> 02:47.439
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:47.440 --> 02:53.949
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:53.950 --> 03:01.580
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:08.500 --> 03:11.050
Grandpa, this rice is funny.

03:12.050 --> 03:15.129
The rice cooker is broken, Bro.

03:15.130 --> 03:16.550
It isn't cooked.

03:24.680 --> 03:27.769
Did you not put enough water in, Grandpa?

03:27.770 --> 03:29.269
Don't be stupid.

03:29.270 --> 03:32.149
Then you must've pressed the wrong button.

03:32.150 --> 03:35.780
You probably hit "warm" instead of "cook."

03:39.280 --> 03:43.540
Would you mind not telling
your mother about this?

03:45.790 --> 03:47.119
What is it?

03:47.120 --> 03:48.289
Hush money.

03:48.290 --> 03:51.959
I'll go buy some takeout
with it and do some shopping.

03:51.960 --> 03:54.049
Seiha, make a shopping list.

03:54.050 --> 03:57.379
Okay! We need bread and strawberries.

03:57.380 --> 03:58.550
I want some hot dogs too!

04:00.180 --> 04:02.309
Why are you staring at me?

04:02.310 --> 04:04.059
I was just impressed.

04:04.060 --> 04:06.979
You're sounding very capable.

04:06.980 --> 04:10.309
Did you think I couldn't do
anything but play baseball?

04:10.310 --> 04:12.319
It was meant as a compliment.

04:12.320 --> 04:14.479
It's not that you can't do anything.

04:14.480 --> 04:17.819
You've just never tried
to do anything else.

04:17.820 --> 04:18.945
Bread

04:17.820 --> 04:18.945
Strawberries

04:17.820 --> 04:20.069
I don't need anything else.

04:18.946 --> 04:20.070
Hot dogs

04:20.070 --> 04:23.829
Takumi, don't be a
person chosen by baseball.

04:23.830 --> 04:26.080
Be a person who chooses baseball.

04:26.450 --> 04:27.579
What does that mean?

04:27.580 --> 04:31.580
Do you know what's out there in the world?

04:32.840 --> 04:39.339
You have no idea what you
can and can't do, do you?

04:39.340 --> 04:47.340
Once you know that, if you still want to play
baseball, then you can say you chose it yourself.

04:47.350 --> 04:51.350
Hey, should we get milk and ramen too?

05:01.070 --> 05:02.990
It's okay, Grandpa.

05:03.320 --> 05:05.490
He's not mad at you.

05:06.160 --> 05:07.449
That right?

05:07.450 --> 05:10.960
I thought I might've crossed a line again.

05:11.290 --> 05:13.459
That was really cool, though.

05:13.460 --> 05:15.459
Huh? It was cool?

05:15.460 --> 05:16.460
Yeah!

05:16.461 --> 05:22.010
You're the coolest when you're
talking about baseball with Bro.

05:27.890 --> 05:30.940
There's something I want to ask you, Shun.

05:31.810 --> 05:32.939
What is it?

05:32.940 --> 05:37.190
Do you really think
that I can't beat Harada?

05:38.070 --> 05:39.439
Are you stupid?

05:39.440 --> 05:42.700
Your weakness is that naivety of yours.

05:43.110 --> 05:46.279
It doesn't matter what I think.

05:46.280 --> 05:48.409
You should learn from the princess.

05:48.410 --> 05:50.709
He only believes in himself.

05:50.710 --> 05:57.209
But you're the only one who knows
all my faults and still believes in me.

05:57.210 --> 05:59.589
I never believed in you.

05:59.590 --> 06:04.260
I mean, who's gonna believe in
someone who punched them in the face?

06:06.970 --> 06:10.729
I heard you turned down
the sports scholarship.

06:10.730 --> 06:13.809
Where did you hear that from?

06:13.810 --> 06:15.899
Was it my mom?

06:15.900 --> 06:18.229
I bet she went to complain to your mom.

06:18.230 --> 06:21.109
You could've gotten into
any school you wanted.

06:21.110 --> 06:23.990
So why pick one without a baseball team?

06:24.610 --> 06:28.869
Because I don't want to play
baseball in high school too.

06:28.870 --> 06:31.750
Then what are you going to do? Play soccer?

06:32.620 --> 06:33.580
Nothing.

06:33.580 --> 06:34.580
Nothing?

06:35.170 --> 06:38.000
You're going to spend
three years doing nothing?

06:38.420 --> 06:39.549
That's right.

06:39.550 --> 06:44.010
I'm planning on just hanging
around and doing nothing.

06:48.300 --> 06:50.220
That sounds pretty rough.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.480
Maybe.

06:53.850 --> 06:56.979
Do you really hate baseball that much?

06:56.980 --> 06:59.149
No. I don't hate it.

06:59.150 --> 07:00.610
I still love it.

07:02.070 --> 07:02.940
Does it hurt?

07:02.941 --> 07:05.069
Of course it hurts!

07:05.070 --> 07:10.949
I'd like to meet the guy who's fine
after getting hit by a huge oaf like you.

07:10.950 --> 07:12.789
Sorry about that.

07:12.790 --> 07:15.919
Apologizing isn't going
to help it hurt any less.

07:15.920 --> 07:18.210
You violent types are such trouble.

07:19.920 --> 07:23.300
You're the only person
I've ever felt like hitting.

07:23.670 --> 07:25.550
Shun, why?

07:27.680 --> 07:30.639
You provoked me.

07:30.640 --> 07:34.180
It was different than usual.
You really pushed me.

07:34.640 --> 07:38.019
You wanted me to hit you, didn't you?

07:38.020 --> 07:39.150
But why?

07:41.110 --> 07:43.569
You got me.

07:43.570 --> 07:47.820
You're not as dumb as I thought you were.

07:57.420 --> 07:58.420
Harada.

08:02.710 --> 08:05.170
I didn't know you were so popular.

08:06.550 --> 08:07.430
The flowers.

08:07.431 --> 08:08.929
Stupid.

08:08.930 --> 08:11.679
These are from Nonomura, not a girl.

08:11.680 --> 08:16.599
It's customary for the new captain
to give flowers to the former one.

08:16.600 --> 08:17.940
I didn't know that.

08:18.480 --> 08:21.519
Everyone clapped for us.

08:21.520 --> 08:24.690
You and Yoshisada were
the only ones not there.

08:25.230 --> 08:26.939
Yoshisada wasn't there either?

08:26.940 --> 08:32.659
Apparently he fell asleep during the ceremony,
so he was getting an earful from a teacher.

08:32.660 --> 08:33.950
That's so like him, huh?

08:34.990 --> 08:36.330
It sure is.

08:38.960 --> 08:40.789
Are you serious?

08:40.790 --> 08:41.710
What?

08:41.711 --> 08:43.669
About the upcoming game.

08:43.670 --> 08:46.589
Do you think I won't pitch seriously?

08:46.590 --> 08:47.720
No.

08:48.300 --> 08:50.470
Then why ask me that?

08:51.180 --> 08:53.099
I just had a thought.

08:53.100 --> 08:56.470
Harada, have you ever
been serious about anything?

08:58.060 --> 08:59.979
That made you angry, didn't it?

08:59.980 --> 09:02.939
You thought that you would've punched
me if I weren't your upperclassman.

09:02.940 --> 09:04.020
I didn't.

09:04.730 --> 09:07.230
I'll listen to what you have to say.

09:12.450 --> 09:15.159
What do you think about Kadowaki?

09:15.160 --> 09:16.239
Kadowaki?

09:16.240 --> 09:19.249
Do you think he's a
great batter or something?

09:19.250 --> 09:20.410
Yes.

09:21.170 --> 09:22.539
Is that all?

09:22.540 --> 09:23.750
What else is there?

09:24.420 --> 09:27.669
You'll lose, you know.

09:27.670 --> 09:29.919
You mean he'll hit off of me?

09:29.920 --> 09:35.679
I can't really express it well, but I think you and
Nagakura could stand to be a little more afraid.

09:35.680 --> 09:38.139
I mean, you can't win if you don't.

09:38.140 --> 09:39.889
Scared of Kadowaki?

09:39.890 --> 09:41.139
That's right.

09:41.140 --> 09:43.900
He's really serious about this.

09:44.270 --> 09:46.610
You want me to fear
him because he's serious?

09:47.900 --> 09:50.109
Be scared, Harada.

09:50.110 --> 09:52.660
Kadowaki is going to really
come after you this game.

09:53.320 --> 09:56.369
He's not thinking about winning or losing.

09:56.370 --> 09:58.409
He's only coming for you.

09:58.410 --> 10:00.160
I can't be scared.

10:00.790 --> 10:04.539
What good is a pitcher
that's afraid of a batter?

10:04.540 --> 10:06.000
Logically, that's true.

10:07.960 --> 10:11.260
I'm a pitcher, so I won't lose to anybody.

10:18.560 --> 10:20.059
Got rejected, huh?

10:20.060 --> 10:21.429
Coach!

10:21.430 --> 10:24.060
You got totally rejected there, Kaionji.

10:24.440 --> 10:29.319
There was something I had to say to
Harada, but I had trouble expressing it.

10:29.320 --> 10:31.899
It wouldn't have helped anyway.

10:31.900 --> 10:32.820
No?

10:32.821 --> 10:34.609
What did he say?

10:34.610 --> 10:38.489
"I'm a pitcher, so I won't
lose to anybody," was it?

10:38.490 --> 10:39.490
Honestly.

10:39.491 --> 10:41.579
Is that something a
normal 13-year-old says?

10:41.580 --> 10:43.579
What should I do?

10:43.580 --> 10:46.419
You already warned Harada.

10:46.420 --> 10:47.539
That's enough.

10:47.540 --> 10:49.959
You don't need to do anything more.

10:49.960 --> 10:52.719
I honestly think it's amazing.

10:52.720 --> 10:53.969
What is?

10:53.970 --> 10:54.970
You.

10:54.971 --> 10:56.969
Me? Not Harada?

10:56.970 --> 10:59.349
Don't bring him up.

10:59.350 --> 11:02.219
He's just a conceited little brat.

11:02.220 --> 11:04.849
But he's a natural born pitcher...

11:04.850 --> 11:07.809
Mr. Tomura. You have a phone call.

11:07.810 --> 11:10.520
I leave Harada and Nagakura in your hands.

11:09.270 --> 11:11.280
Please return to the faculty office.

11:10.520 --> 11:11.730
Do what you want.

11:12.900 --> 11:14.069
What's wrong?

11:14.070 --> 11:16.569
I'm leaving the whole battery to you.

11:16.570 --> 11:17.989
Does that not satisfy you?

11:17.990 --> 11:19.740
No, it's...

11:20.280 --> 11:24.289
You promised Kadowaki that
Harada would pitch, didn't you?

11:24.290 --> 11:28.129
So I'll leave the battery
under your care until the game.

11:28.130 --> 11:30.170
I won't butt in.

11:39.010 --> 11:40.049
Yes?

11:40.050 --> 11:41.639
<i>Hello, Mizugaki.</i>

11:41.640 --> 11:44.059
Oh, is that you, Kaionji?

11:44.060 --> 11:46.889
<i>I told him he was going to lose.</i>

11:46.890 --> 11:47.980
Huh?

11:48.400 --> 11:51.689
I told Harada that he was going to lose.

11:51.690 --> 11:53.479
That he couldn't beat Kadowaki.

11:53.480 --> 11:56.990
That's something.

11:57.400 --> 11:58.529
<i>What do you think?</i>

11:58.530 --> 11:59.869
<i>Don't you agree?</i>

11:59.870 --> 12:03.700
What's the point of telling
him that before the game?

12:04.160 --> 12:08.919
<i>I believe that the team
who wants it more wins.</i>

12:08.920 --> 12:12.959
<i>There's no way Kadowaki
doesn't want to win this more.</i>

12:12.960 --> 12:14.459
That's true.

12:14.460 --> 12:17.009
Kadowaki only has one goal.

12:17.010 --> 12:20.009
He knows how to focus, that's for sure.

12:20.010 --> 12:23.719
<i>Yeah, but I still think we can win.</i>

12:23.720 --> 12:25.219
<i>What?</i>

12:25.220 --> 12:26.929
I mean, I want to win.

12:26.930 --> 12:28.729
I'd rather win if we're doing this.

12:28.730 --> 12:30.979
And I think we have a chance.

12:30.980 --> 12:33.480
Well, good for you.

12:33.980 --> 12:37.319
<i>I'm thinking about changing Harada.</i>

12:37.320 --> 12:42.029
<i>Maybe I can change the team so
they're able to compete with you guys.</i>

12:42.030 --> 12:42.830
<i>Right?</i>

12:42.831 --> 12:46.499
"Right"? I don't understand
half of what you're saying.

12:46.500 --> 12:51.919
<i>Well, my coach entrusted the battery to me.</i>

12:51.920 --> 12:54.089
<i>So I'm going to do what I can.</i>

12:54.090 --> 12:55.749
<i>We still have a week.</i>

12:55.750 --> 12:56.880
<i>That's enough time, right?</i>

12:57.670 --> 13:00.759
What are you going on about?

13:00.760 --> 13:03.009
To be honest, I'm a little worried.

13:03.010 --> 13:06.969
I wasn't sure if I had
the ability to do this.

13:06.970 --> 13:09.939
So I wondered what you might do.

13:09.940 --> 13:11.269
That's why I called.

13:11.270 --> 13:12.270
Me?

13:15.900 --> 13:17.150
<i>Well, I feel better.</i>

13:17.740 --> 13:21.530
<i>It feels good when you talk
your issues out with someone.</i>

13:22.160 --> 13:23.030
<i>Bye.</i>

13:23.031 --> 13:24.409
Hold on.

13:24.410 --> 13:28.159
Is that really the only reason
you called me? To feel better?

13:28.160 --> 13:31.419
Just tell me what you want to say.

13:31.420 --> 13:34.500
Are you just bragging that your
coach entrusted you with them?

13:35.380 --> 13:36.709
<i>It's a warning.</i>

13:36.710 --> 13:37.630
What?

13:37.631 --> 13:40.760
<i>I'd say it's my declaration of
war against Mizugaki Shunji.</i>

13:41.760 --> 13:43.389
<i>Maybe that's old-fashioned.</i>

13:43.390 --> 13:45.929
There's no way we're losing.

13:45.930 --> 13:48.019
<i>I thought you'd say that.</i>

13:48.020 --> 13:49.929
<i>That's why I called.</i>

13:49.930 --> 13:53.059
<i>You have Kadowaki, and I have our battery.</i>

13:53.060 --> 13:55.440
<i>We each have our weapons.</i>

13:55.900 --> 13:58.529
You just got the chills, didn't you?

13:58.530 --> 14:00.359
Let's do this.

14:00.360 --> 14:02.949
We'll make this the best game ever.

14:02.950 --> 14:04.870
<i>Look here...</i>

14:05.160 --> 14:09.239
Harada getting hit off of,
or Kadowaki striking out.

14:09.240 --> 14:11.120
Which would you rather see?

14:12.790 --> 14:14.329
Both.

14:14.330 --> 14:15.499
<i>Mizugaki.</i>

14:15.500 --> 14:18.299
Shut up, will you?

14:18.300 --> 14:20.879
Don't talk to me like you know me.

14:20.880 --> 14:22.879
That's the Mizugaki I know.

14:22.880 --> 14:25.089
I'm looking forward to what you do.

14:25.090 --> 14:26.390
Bye.

14:31.930 --> 14:32.730
Gather 'round.

14:32.731 --> 14:34.060
Okay.

14:35.440 --> 14:40.070
I want to be in peak
condition for our game.

14:40.570 --> 14:43.149
Officially, it's just an exhibition game.

14:43.150 --> 14:46.820
But this is our game. One we made happen.

14:47.200 --> 14:49.369
That's the type of game
we can end things on.

14:49.370 --> 14:52.330
I'm really excited about it all.

14:52.960 --> 14:56.080
But that's just how us seniors see it.

14:56.630 --> 15:00.090
We're thankful for the help
of all you underclassmen.

15:00.670 --> 15:03.130
I know this is long past due.

15:05.090 --> 15:07.849
I don't think you gotta worry about it.

15:07.850 --> 15:12.599
I'm just here because it sounds
like more fun than regular practice.

15:12.600 --> 15:15.100
How's it different from regular practice?

15:15.390 --> 15:18.729
We get to choose our own drills, right?

15:18.730 --> 15:23.029
I bet you like that you have less work to...

15:23.030 --> 15:24.030
Idiot!

15:24.450 --> 15:26.360
But practice is fun.

15:27.160 --> 15:29.620
Kaionji, that's how we feel.

15:29.990 --> 15:31.910
We're here to help and have fun.

15:40.290 --> 15:41.290
Takumi.

15:42.550 --> 15:45.219
You were pitching for
batting practice all day.

15:45.220 --> 15:46.380
Why did you hold back?

15:47.970 --> 15:50.719
You don't need to go all-out today?

15:50.720 --> 15:52.139
I can see it on your face.

15:52.140 --> 15:53.269
See what?

15:53.270 --> 15:54.640
You're hungry.

15:55.560 --> 15:57.099
You haven't been yourself lately.

15:57.100 --> 15:58.400
How so?

15:58.770 --> 16:03.360
I've been waiting for you to tell me to
catch for you because you want to pitch.

16:04.070 --> 16:05.320
So why haven't you?

16:06.650 --> 16:08.160
It's not like you.

16:12.330 --> 16:13.330
Harada.

16:14.040 --> 16:16.119
We need you to pitch.

16:16.120 --> 16:17.159
Nonomura.

16:17.160 --> 16:19.420
Get the underclassmen to defend.

16:34.640 --> 16:35.890
Strike.

16:45.230 --> 16:46.360
Strike.

16:52.490 --> 16:54.740
Strike three. You're out.

16:58.830 --> 16:59.750
Nagakura.

16:59.750 --> 17:00.750
Yes?

17:01.250 --> 17:02.999
Could someone other than you catch it?

17:03.000 --> 17:04.129
Huh?

17:04.130 --> 17:05.249
Nonomura.

17:05.250 --> 17:06.250
Yes.

17:08.510 --> 17:12.009
Go hit some balls for them to field.

17:12.010 --> 17:13.010
Got it.

17:14.560 --> 17:15.889
Kaionji.

17:15.890 --> 17:17.770
What did you mean by that?

17:18.180 --> 17:19.519
I meant exactly what I said.

17:19.520 --> 17:21.269
What?

17:21.270 --> 17:25.769
I asked you if someone other than
you could catch Harada's pitches.

17:25.770 --> 17:27.989
No, I don't think so.

17:27.990 --> 17:29.989
Even with practice?

17:29.990 --> 17:32.279
Not in time for our game against Yokote.

17:32.280 --> 17:35.159
That's a composed answer, Nagakura.

17:35.160 --> 17:38.249
Are you trying to make me panic?

17:38.250 --> 17:42.539
Look, could you play catcher
if Harada's not pitching to you?

17:42.540 --> 17:45.339
Yes, of course.

17:45.340 --> 17:46.920
I could catch for anyone.

17:47.550 --> 17:49.760
You could catch for anyone?

17:50.670 --> 17:52.300
Let me ask you again.

17:52.760 --> 17:56.309
Could you still play with the same
feeling with a different pitcher?

17:56.310 --> 17:57.470
That's...

17:58.180 --> 17:59.429
Well...

17:59.430 --> 18:00.890
I didn't think so.

18:01.980 --> 18:02.980
No.

18:03.150 --> 18:05.940
Sorry for being so hard on you.

18:07.400 --> 18:08.819
If that's all, I should...

18:08.820 --> 18:10.069
What about Harada?

18:10.070 --> 18:10.740
Huh?

18:10.741 --> 18:14.320
Could he still pitch if
you're not the catcher?

18:14.780 --> 18:15.820
Captain.

18:16.330 --> 18:19.490
I hope he can.

18:21.080 --> 18:23.289
That's what a real pitcher is.

18:23.290 --> 18:24.749
That's just theory.

18:24.750 --> 18:25.999
Nagakura.

18:26.000 --> 18:30.130
You have to be more free,
or you won't be able to continue baseball.

18:34.380 --> 18:35.340
Let's go.

18:35.341 --> 18:37.350
Harada said he'd give
you a ride on his bike.

18:44.560 --> 18:46.689
I heard you're giving me a ride.

18:46.690 --> 18:48.819
No, I'm getting in back.

18:48.820 --> 18:51.570
What? So I'm pedaling?

18:55.530 --> 18:56.530
Gou.

18:57.780 --> 19:00.330
What were you talking about with Kaionji?

19:02.500 --> 19:04.580
What did you stop for?

19:05.250 --> 19:07.579
Kadowaki sure is amazing.

19:07.580 --> 19:09.840
Yeah, as I batter, I guess.

19:10.880 --> 19:12.709
Not just as a batter.

19:12.710 --> 19:15.429
I mean, he already went to nationals.

19:15.430 --> 19:18.350
Yet he's going out of his way
to play some no-name team.

19:19.050 --> 19:20.680
Isn't that amazing?

19:21.310 --> 19:22.350
I don't know.

19:23.850 --> 19:26.269
You really don't know?

19:26.270 --> 19:27.270
Yeah.

19:27.480 --> 19:31.270
Do you think it's a given that
Kadowaki would be worried?

19:32.110 --> 19:33.860
I don't think anything of it.

19:36.780 --> 19:39.949
Could you pitch if I weren't your catcher?

19:39.950 --> 19:40.989
I could.

19:40.990 --> 19:41.990
I see.

19:42.450 --> 19:48.380
Everyone keeps asking me that,
but it's got nothing to do with anything.

19:49.130 --> 19:51.879
Nothing really matters to you, does it?

19:51.880 --> 19:52.999
That's not it.

19:53.000 --> 19:54.379
It is.

19:54.380 --> 19:58.140
I don't care if you're not my catcher.

20:01.560 --> 20:03.099
You can borrow my bike.

20:03.100 --> 20:04.139
Just ride it home.

20:04.140 --> 20:05.390
Thanks.

20:05.980 --> 20:11.900
If someone can catch my pitches as well as you
can, then I've got no problem pitching to them.

20:12.860 --> 20:14.149
I know.

20:14.150 --> 20:18.240
So I'm not with you
because you're a catcher.

20:19.660 --> 20:23.159
If they're good enough, I
don't care who my catcher is.

20:23.160 --> 20:25.790
You don't care, huh?

20:28.250 --> 20:30.039
I think I just realized something.

20:30.040 --> 20:31.040
What?

20:31.790 --> 20:34.499
You've never caught a ball
thrown by Harada Takumi.

20:34.500 --> 20:35.170
Huh?

20:35.171 --> 20:36.549
That's right.

20:36.550 --> 20:40.180
You're the only person who
can never catch your own pitch.

20:40.760 --> 20:43.309
What kind of nonsense is that?

20:43.310 --> 20:44.680
It's a pity.

20:45.390 --> 20:47.769
You'll never know something so vital.

20:47.770 --> 20:52.360
I'm the only one who knows how
it feels to catch one of your pitches.

20:53.480 --> 20:54.480
I'm not giving that up.

20:55.150 --> 20:56.400
Not to anyone.

20:58.240 --> 20:59.240
Gou.

20:59.950 --> 21:04.450
I want to try to climb a
tree once our game is over.

21:05.120 --> 21:06.700
Tree? What tree?

21:07.040 --> 21:09.210
The big one by Sawaguchi's place.

21:12.580 --> 21:14.710
Climbing a tree is pretty hard, you know.

21:15.000 --> 21:16.000
Later.

21:21.800 --> 21:24.160
Summer's peak came and went

21:26.520 --> 21:32.849
That's what the weather report said

21:32.850 --> 21:39.360
But it still feels like
the city is restless

21:47.200 --> 21:55.200
The evening bells of 5 p.m.
resonate inside my heart today

22:02.130 --> 22:08.535
Clouding me with something
convenient like "destiny"

22:20.511 --> 22:24.199
It's the final fireworks of the year

22:24.200 --> 22:27.910
I will remember them for years to come

22:27.911 --> 22:31.619
I will remember them for years to come

22:31.620 --> 22:33.455
Are you here? You're probably not

22:33.456 --> 22:35.289
Are you here? You're probably not

22:35.290 --> 22:37.190
I'm sure you're not

22:37.191 --> 22:39.089
I'm sure you're not

22:39.090 --> 22:40.905
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:40.906 --> 22:42.719
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:42.720 --> 22:45.535
I close my eyes and dream

23:23.120 --> 23:28.080
Episode 11: "Their Spring"
